# Fake Stripe-pass backend used ONLY by the GOLD-09 entitlement harness
# (hostv2/e2e/thePassSurvivesTheWebhookRace.spec.mjs). The host never resolves;
# every request is intercepted by Playwright. No real backend, no real keys,
# and no charge can be taken against this bundle.
#
# WHY ITS OWN BUNDLE, and it is a harder requirement than GOLD-07's.
# passGate.js opens EVERY gate while `isBillingLive()` is false, and that
# predicate needs BOTH a truthy REACT_APP_API_BASE_URL and an explicit
# REACT_APP_BILLING_LIVE === '1'. The ordinary e2e build carries neither, so
# against the shared bundle the paywall is dormant by design: the refresh
# effect returns on its first line, `passHeld` is never consulted, and a spec
# written there would pass without executing one line of the entitlement path.
# That is precisely how GOLD-09 stayed open while `passGate.test.js` and
# `passEntitlement.test.js` were both green — the unit suites drive the module,
# and nothing drove the SHELL.
#
# NOT baked into the shared bundle, deliberately, and this one is not merely
# noisy but dangerous: REACT_APP_BILLING_LIVE=1 is the live-money switch. D-2's
# five preconditions govern flipping it for real. It belongs to a throwaway
# harness bundle or to production, never to the suite every other spec runs on.
REACT_APP_API_BASE_URL=https://passgate-mock.invalid
# The live-money switch, in a bundle whose API host cannot resolve and whose
# every request Playwright intercepts. This is the only place in the repo it is
# set to 1.
REACT_APP_BILLING_LIVE=1
